Saturday, September 3, 1994.  While others go about thier Labor
Day fling, our hero sits down in front of his computer and begins
the final stretch.

Two pots of coffee later, after a package of Twinkies, a Taco
Bell bean burrito, two grilled cheese sandwiches (slightly
burnt), and a few handfuls of Andy Capp's Hot Fries later, he
prepares the next package for the masses...

This version skips over 0.1.4 simply because 0.1.4 was going in a
totally different direction.  There were some serious bugs in
0.1.3, which 0.1.4 was built on, and I decided that I needed to
go back to the source of the problem to get at them.  After I
clobbered them, I also set out to speed things up a bit.  The
product you hold in your hands now has no really new features,
but is faster, less damaging, and potentially more stable.

NOW I think I can get back into the new features!

